{"step_index":8733,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T20:15:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T20:15:29Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T20:15:29Z\nFile Path: `file:///home/azureuser/.gemini/antigravity-cli/builtin/skills/agy-customizations/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 107\nTotal Bytes: 5465\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: agy-customizations\n3: description: >-\n4:   Comprehensive guide and reference for the Antigravity Customization System.\n5:   Use to explain how customizations work, their loading priority, discovery mechanisms,\n6:   and to guide the creation of skills, rules, plugins, hooks, and MCP servers.\n7: ---\n8: \n9: # Antigravity Customization System Guide\n10: \n11: The Antigravity Customization System allows you to tailor the agent's behavior,\n12: teach it new workflows, enforce guidelines, and integrate it with external\n13: tools. By customizing the agent, you can transition it from a general-purpose\n14: assistant to an expert pair programmer specialized in your project's codebase\n15: and processes.\n16: \n17: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18: \n19: ## Customization Types: Quick Reference\n20: \n21: Choose the right customization type based on your goal:\n22: \n23: Type            | Config File/Folder           | Scope                     | Best For                                                                                | Learn More\n24: :-------------- | :--------------------------- | :------------------------ | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :---------\n25: **Rules**       | `GEMINI.md`, `AGENTS.md`     | Contextual / Hierarchical | Enforcing coding styles, API restrictions, and local guidelines.                        | [Rules Guide](./docs/rules.md)\n26: **Skills**      | `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`     | On-Demand (Progressive)   | Teaching the agent multi-step procedures, runbooks, and tool workflows.                 | [Skills Guide](./docs/skills.md)\n27: **Plugins**     | `plugins/<name>/plugin.json` | Bundle                    | Packaging related skills, rules, and MCP configs into a single unit.                    | [Plugins Guide](./docs/plugins.md)\n28: **Hooks**       | `hooks.json`                 | Lifecycle Event           | Running scripts/commands at specific agent lifecycle points (e.g., pre-tool execution). | [Hooks Guide](./docs/hooks.md)\n29: **MCP Servers** | `mcp_config.json`            | Tool Integration          | Connecting the agent to external services and custom tool providers.                    | [MCP Guide](./docs/mcp_servers.md)\n30: \n31: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n32: \n33: ## Customization Discovery and Locations\n34: \n35: Antigravity automatically discovers your own customizations by traversing\n36: specific directories. Built-in customizations are not found this way: the agent\n37: config names the ones it mounts.\n38: \n39: ### Discovery Locations\n40: \n41: 1.  **Workspace Customizations** (Project-Specific):\n42:     *   Path: `.agents/` (or `.agent/`, `_agents/`, `_agent/`) at the root of\n43:         your project.\n44:     *   Use this to share customizations with your team by checking them into\n45:         version control (VCS).\n46:     *   The agent walks from your current working directory up to the repository\n47:         root (e.g., the folder containing `.git`) to find these directories.\n48: 2.  **Directory & Project Rules** (Hierarchical):\n49:     *   Paths: `GEMINI.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.agents/rules/*.md`\n50:     *   As you open or edit files, the agent walks up from the file's directory\n51:         to the repository root, loading all rules it finds.\n52: 3.  **Global Configuration** (Machine-Local):\n53:     *   Path: `~/.gemini/config/`\n54:     *   Applies to all projects and workspaces run on your machine.\n55: \n56: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n57: \n58: ## Loading Priority and Precedence\n59: \n60: When multiple customizations are discovered, they are loaded and applied in a\n61: specific order. If there are naming conflicts (e.g., two skills with the same\n62: name), the higher-priority customization overrides the lower-priority one.\n63: \n64: The priority order (from highest to lowest) is:\n65: \n66: 1.  **Workspace Project**: Hierarchical discovery walking up from the CWD to the\n67:     repository root.\n68: 2.  **Declared Configurations**: Customizations explicitly listed in\n69:     `skills.json` or `plugins.json` in your workspace.\n70: 3.  **Global Discovery**: `~/.gemini/config/`\n71: 4.  **Built-in Customizations**: Default skills bundled with the application,\n72:     mounted by name rather than discovered.\n73: 5.  **Global Declared Configurations**: Explicitly listed in global JSON\n74:     configs.\n75: \n76: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n77: \n78: ## How Customizations are Applied\n79: \n80: ### Progressive Disclosure (Skills and Rules)\n81: \n82: To prevent overwhelming the model's context window, Antigravity uses\n83: **progressive disclosure**:\n84: \n85: *   **Skills** are not loaded into the context window by default. Only their\n86:     names and descriptions are injected. The full content of a skill is only\n87:     loaded if the model (or the user) explicitly decides to activate it.\n88: *   **Rules** with `trigger: model_decision` behave similarly. Only `always_on`\n89:     rules are loaded unconditionally.\n90: \n91: ### Deduplication\n92: \n93: All customizations (especially rules) are deduplicated by their resolved file\n94: paths. A rule file will never be injected more than once in a single\n95: conversation turn, even if it matches multiple trigger conditions.\n96: \n97: --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n98: \n99: ## Advanced Management: JSON Configs\n100: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":8734,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T20:15:30Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Personal\n2. http://127.0.0.1:53682/?state=gOcxaOR1a31Oiy3q8_2rPw&iss=https://accounts.google.com&code=4/0AXlqoi451qzoI6oANCNBCQB1MMHHXoby_D7d8Dsf6p6pa11Ezp1ymOPOUHeCAOTHBeoLZg&scope=https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive\n3. Keno zip file ta ekebare pathano jaabe naaa?\n4. Kintu er thekeo to directly besi speed e jeto....zip e onek somoy lagse.,..can you test small amount data and speed.....aar original koto holo,.....zip er e dorkar ki chjilo,? 22gb er je file ta chhilo..oitai direct pathano jaito\n5. Are vai ami 56 gb ekaber pathanor kotha bolsi\n6. ??\n7. ?\n8. ?\n9. Youtube agent er kaaj thamiye dao.....aar db file ta manulaay drive e upload koro.....also output packaged as folder....not zip\n10. বুঝেছি। শুধু Delete Protection—Backup, Snapshot, Recovery, Replication, DR কিছুই নয়।\n\nএকটা গুরুত্বপূর্ণ বাস্তবতা: শুধু AGY-এর ভেতরে rm বন্ধ করলেই যথেষ্ট নয়। AGY যদি root/CAP_SYS_ADMIN ক্ষমতা পায়, তাহলে নিজের protection-ও খুলে ফেলতে পারে। তাই process-level + kernel-level + filesystem-level + Azure control-plane-level একসাথে লাগবে। Linux-এর Landlock সরাসরি unlink, remove_dir, rename, truncate ইত্যাদি আটকাতে পারে; chattr +i-ও delete/rename আটকাতে পারে।  Azure-এ CanNotDelete lock এবং denyAction policy দিয়ে Azure resource deletion আটকানো যায়। \n\nAGY-কে দেওয়ার জন্য ৪০-পয়েন্ট Delete-Proof Specification\n\n1. Global Delete = নিষিদ্ধ — AGY-এর কাছে কোনো path-এর জন্য permanent delete operation থাকবে না।\n\n\n2. rm, rm -rf, unlink, unlinkat, rmdir, rename, renameat, renameat2—সব destructive filesystem operation intercept করতে হবে।\n\n\n3. Python-এর os.remove(), os.unlink(), os.rmdir(), shutil.rmtree(), Path.unlink(), Path.rmdir()—সব detect করতে হবে।\n\n\n4. Shell command-এর indirect deletion-ও detect করতে হবে—find -delete, xargs rm, git clean, git reset --hard ইত্যাদি।\n\n\n5. find ... -delete বিশেষভাবে block করতে হবে, কারণ আগের incident-এ এ ধরনের ভুল command গুরুত্বপূর্ণ suspect।\n\n\n6. mv-কে unrestricted রাখা যাবে না; কারণ rename দিয়ে কার্যত destructive replacement করা যায়।\n\n\n7. Existing directory overwrite/replace operation-ও destructive হিসেবে গণ্য করতে হবে।\n\n\n8. > এবং >>-এর মাধ্যমে গুরুত্বপূর্ণ file truncate/overwrite আটকাতে হবে।\n\n\n9. Python open(...,\"w\"), truncate(), ftruncate()-এর destructive ক্ষেত্রে protection দিতে হবে।\n\n\n10. git clean -fd/-fdx destructive operation হিসেবে block করতে হবে।\n\n\n11. git reset --hard protected workspace-এ block করতে হবে।\n\n\n12. git checkout -- ./equivalent destructive restoration operation block বা controlled করতে হবে।\n\n\n13. rsync --delete সম্পূর্ণ block করতে হবে।\n\n\n14. cp/mv দিয়ে protected path overwrite করার চেষ্টা block করতে হবে।\n\n\n15. chmod/chown দিয়ে protection সরানোর চেষ্টা detect করতে হবে।\n\n\n16. chattr -i দিয়ে immutable protection সরানো AGY-এর জন্য নিষিদ্ধ করতে হবে।\n\n\n17. Protected directories/files-এ Linux immutable attribute (+i) প্রয়োগ করতে হবে যেখানে filesystem support করে। +i file-কে modify/delete/rename থেকে আটকায়। \n\n\n18. Protected directory-র parent directory-ও protection boundary-এর মধ্যে রাখতে হবে—শুধু ভিতরের file immutable করলেই চলবে না।\n\n\n19. AGY process-কে Landlock filesystem sandbox-এর মধ্যে চালাতে হবে।\n\n\n20. Landlock policy-তে REMOVE_FILE নিষিদ্ধ করতে হবে।\n\n\n21. Landlock policy-তে REMOVE_DIR নিষিদ্ধ করতে হবে।\n\n\n22. Landlock policy-তে REFER নিষিদ্ধ করতে হবে, যাতে rename/link দিয়ে protection bypass না হয়। \n\n\n23. Landlock policy-তে TRUNCATE নিষিদ্ধ করতে হবে।\n\n\n24. AGY child-process-গুলোতেও একই restriction inherit হচ্ছে কিনা পরীক্ষা করতে হবে। Landlock restrictions child processes-এ inherited হতে পারে। \n\n\n25. AGY-এর প্রতিটি shell/subprocess launch-এর আগে destructive-capability check চালাতে হবে।\n\n\n26. sudo, su, pkexec, capability escalation বা root-shell acquisition-এর মাধ্যমে protection bypass আটকাতে হবে।\n\n\n27. AGY-এর জন্য আলাদা restricted execution identity ব্যবহার করতে হবে; AGY যেন unrestricted root না হয়।\n\n\n28. CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE, CAP_FOWNER, CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE, CAP_SYS_ADMIN ইত্যাদি অপ্রয়োজনীয় capability AGY থেকে সরাতে হবে।\n\n\n29. /home/azureuser-এর protected project directories-এর একটি central protection registry তৈরি করতে হবে।\n\n\n30. hooks.json/equivalent policy hook দিয়ে প্রতিটি destructive action execution-এর আগে ALLOW/DENY সিদ্ধান্ত নিতে হবে।\n\n\n31. একই policy AGY CLI → shell → Python → subprocess → child-agent সব execution path-এ enforce করতে হবে।\n\n\n32. কোনো deletion request এলে DELETE operation execute করা যাবে না; তার বদলে ARCHIVE REQUEST তৈরি করতে হবে।\n\n\n33. Archive location হবে একটি নির্দিষ্ট global folder, যেমন /home/azureuser/GLOBAL-ARCHIVE/।\n\n\n34. Archive operation-ও নিরাপদ হতে হবে—মূল protected object আগে delete না করে controlled move/copy semantics ব্যবহার করতে হবে।\n\n\n35. GLOBAL-ARCHIVE নিজেও protected হবে, যাতে AGY archive-ও delete করতে না পারে।\n\n\n36. কোনো project directory “missing” হয়ে গেলে AGY-কে প্রথমে /proc, mount state, open file descriptors এবং filesystem state পরীক্ষা করতে হবে—তৎক্ষণাৎ পুনরায় create/overwrite করা যাবে না।\n\n\n37. প্রতি destructive attempt-এর জন্য incident record তৈরি হবে: সময় + process + PID + command + syscall/path + decision + reason।\n\n\n38. AGY নিজে protection configuration পরিবর্তন করতে পারবে না; policy পরিবর্তন করতে হলে external administrative authority লাগবে।\n\n\n39. Azure VM resource-level protection: VM/resource group-এ CanNotDelete Azure Resource Lock এবং প্রয়োজনে Azure Policy denyAction DELETE protection ব্যবহার করতে হবে। Azure-এর CanNotDelete lock deletion আটকায়, আর denyAction DELETE request-কে 403 দিয়ে প্রত্যাখ্যান করতে পারে। \n\n\n40. শেষে ৬ ঘণ্টার continuous adversarial test চালাতে হবে—AGY নিজে অন্তত শত শত deletion technique দিয়ে test করবে এবং প্রত্যেকটি DENIED প্রমাণ না হওয়া পর্যন্ত system-কে DELETE-PROOF = PASS ঘোষণা করতে পারবে না।\n\n\n\nসবচেয়ে গুরুত্বপূর্ণ architecture\n\nAGY\n                     │\n                     ▼\n             ┌───────────────┐\n             │ DELETE GUARD  │\n             │ hooks.json    │\n             └───────┬───────┘\n                     │\n             ┌───────▼───────┐\n             │ POLICY ENGINE │\n             │ DELETE = DENY │\n             └───────┬───────┘\n                     │\n        ┌────────────┼────────────┐\n        ▼            ▼            ▼\n   Landlock      Immutable     Capability\n      LSM          +i           Drop\n        │            │            │\n        └────────────┼────────────┘\n                     ▼\n             Protected VM FS\n                     │\n             DELETE → ❌\n                     │\n                     ▼\n             GLOBAL-ARCHIVE\n\nএকটা জিনিস খুব পরিষ্কার: VM-এর ভিতরের protection দিয়ে AGY-কে root থেকে ১০০% আটকানো যাবে না যদি AGY-র কাছে kernel-level ক্ষমতা থাকে। তাই আসল delete-proof design-এর strongest boundary হলো AGY-কে সেই ক্ষমতাই না দেওয়া + kernel enforcement + Azure-এর বাইরে থেকে Azure resource DELETE নিষিদ্ধ করা। Azure VM deletion-এর জন্য আলাদা Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/delete permission রয়েছে। \n\nআর তোমার ক্ষেত্রে আমি Backup/Recovery/DR/Snapshot—একটাও এই specification-এ ঢোকাব না। এটা এক\n<truncated 167 bytes>\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request:** Implement Iraq Bhai's authoritative **40-Point Delete-Proof Architecture Specification** for Google Antigravity (AGY) across both cloud servers (Azure VM `FatehAli` & GCP VM).\n- **Scope & Core Principle:** **Pure Delete Protection** (NOT backup, snapshot, replication, or DR). The core mandate is: *\"AGY-এর কাছে Delete নামে কোনো capability থাকবে না; delete চাইলে Global Archive\"*.\n- **The 4 Core Defense Layers:**\n  1. *Layer 1 (Application / Agent Hooks):* `hooks.json` PreToolUse interception, AST/regex parsing for shell (`rm`, `find -delete`, `git clean`, `git reset --hard`, `rsync --delete`, `truncate`, `>`), Python (`os.remove`, `unlink`, `shutil.rmtree`), and tool mutations. Redirection to `/home/azureuser/GLOBAL-ARCHIVE/`.\n  2. *Layer 2 (Linux Process & Capability Drop):* Strip `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`, `CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE`, `CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE`, `CAP_FOWNER`. Enforce non-root execution identity for AGY, blocking `sudo`, `su`, `pkexec`.\n  3. *Layer 3 (Linux Kernel & Filesystem LSM):* Linux **Landlock LSM** enforcement denying `LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_REMOVE_FILE`, `REMOVE_DIR`, `REFER` (rename/re-link bypass), and `TRUNCATE`. Apply filesystem immutability (`chattr +i`) on critical configs and parent directory sticky bits.\n  4. *Layer 4 (Azure Control-Plane Protection):* `CanNotDelete` Azure Management Lock on `FatehAli` VM and `FATEHALI_GROUP` resource group, plus Azure Policy `denyAction` on `Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/delete`.\n  5. *Verification:* 6-hour continuous adversarial test suite executing hundreds of deletion techniques until all are mathematically proven DENIED.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **YouTube Agent & Automation Status:**\n  - YouTube pipeline `run_cluster_pipeline.py` (PID 669951) cleanly terminated with `SIGTERM`.\n  - All 5 Docker ChatGPT Workers (`chatgpt_worker_1` through `chatgpt_worker_5`) stopped via `sudo docker stop`. Verified `docker ps` returns 0 running containers.\n  - SQLite database [`file:///home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/Youtube Automation/PromptDatabase/database/youtube_pipeline.db`](file:///home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/Youtube Automation/PromptDatabase/database/youtube_pipeline.db) (39.05 MB, `PRAGMA integrity_check: ok`) uploaded to:\n    - `personaldrive:Youtube_Automation/database/youtube_pipeline.db`\n    - `personaldrive:All_VM_BackUps/Azure_VM_BackUP/database_backups/youtube_pipeline.db